  "name": "Ojapali (Assamese chorus narrative)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ojapali is an Assamese chorus-narrative form, strongest in Darrang district, in which a lead singer (oja) sings and narrates episodes while a principal assistant (daina pali) comments and banters and the other palis sing refrains, clash small khuti taal cymbals and dance. Suknanni ojapali sings the Manasa (snake goddess) cycle of Sukavi Narayandev, and byah-gowa ojapali draws on the Ramayana and Mahabharata. The manjira card stands in for the khuti taal.",
